{
 "encounter_id": "00827",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "FAMILY_MEMBER"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, please, my husband, he ate prawns, and now his lips are swelling, and he's coming out in hives!"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Bring him straight in, sit him up. Sir, can you tell me your name, and how you're feeling? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Peter. My lips feel huge. And my throat's a bit tight."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When did you eat the prawns?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Twenty minutes ago. A prawn curry, at the Thai place."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, it was ten minutes. We'd only just got to the car, I looked at my watch. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It doesn't matter exactly, we're acting now. Any trouble breathing?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Not really. I'm fine, I can breathe."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He's wheezing, doctor, listen to him."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll listen. Have you had a reaction like this before? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Never. I've eaten prawns all my life. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies to medicines or other foods, as far as you know?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "None. I've never had any."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. Pulse, oxygen, pressure. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Please hurry. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 112, blood pressure 102 over 60, oxygen 95 percent, temperature 36.8, respiratory rate 22.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is that bad? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your pulse is fast, the oxygen is a little low, and the pressure is on the low side, which is concerning. Open your mouth, Peter. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ahh.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your lips and tongue are swollen, there are raised red hives over your chest and arms, and I can hear a wheeze in your chest."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it serious? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, it's what we call anaphylaxis, a severe reaction to the prawns. We're treating it now."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Oh God. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Nurse, I want you to give adrenaline, intramuscular, point five of a milligram, into his thigh, now. And oxygen, and a drip."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will I be all right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes. The adrenaline works fast. You'll feel your heart race for a few minutes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Can I stay with him? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, please, hold his hand. I'm also going to give an antihistamine and a steroid by injection, and we'll keep you in for at least six hours, to watch for a second reaction."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'd like a blood test for tryptase, which shows the reaction, and a repeat set of observations every fifteen minutes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Thank you, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Peter, don't eat or drink anything, and tell the nurse if your breathing worsens."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. ~"
  }
 ],
